# Local Libraries

This project intentionally uses local libraries from `lib/` for the motor
output chain. PlatformIO discovers these before external dependencies, which
keeps the flight build reproducible.

## Libraries

| Library | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `DShotRMT` | ESP-IDF 5 RMT DShot driver with patched bidirectional DShot receive, GCR/eRPM decode, persistent RX/TX buffers, and telemetry stats. |
| `easy-esc-esp32` | Local EasyESC facade used by the firmware. Exposes cached `EasyEscMotor::telemetry()` so RPM filtering can read BDShot eRPM without reaching into driver internals. |

## Rules For Motor-Library Changes

- Do not allocate in the flight-loop send/telemetry path.
- Do not attach, detach, delete, or recreate RMT channels during normal motor
  output. Passthrough suspend/resume is the exception.
- Normal DShot output must continue even when telemetry is missing or bad.
- Bad BDShot frames must increment counters, not publish a new RPM value.
- Keep DShot300 as the safe default unless a bench capture proves a higher
  speed is reliable on the actual wiring.

## PlatformIO Dependency Note

`platformio.ini` no longer lists the EasyESC GitHub dependency directly for the
flight/test envs. The local `lib/easy-esc-esp32` copy is the source of truth for
this firmware because it contains the BDShot telemetry bridge.
